        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-04T04:18:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It will be soon. We're initially launching on Google Play. Our next immediate goals are Android phone support, Amazon Appstore, and official artwork.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I saw your note in the other thread about official artwork driving sales, &nbsp;but for my $2.49 (already happily paid) I'd rather have Vengeance support before art. &nbsp;The Sentinels and V5 can be a real pain to manage in the normal method, so I'm more likely to use the app for them than for any other scenario. &nbsp; Or, I would be, &nbsp;if I could <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
